#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:71
msgid ""
"Write a node that logs at each severity level as a simulated battery drains. "
"This node gives you controlled messages to inspect with the CLI in the later "
"steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:74
msgid ""
"In the package module directory ``battery_logging/battery_logging``, create "
"a file named ``battery_monitor.py``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:76
msgid "In the ``battery_monitor.py`` file, include the following code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:78
msgid ""
"import rclpy\n"
"from rclpy.node import Node\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"class BatteryMonitor(Node):\n"
"\n"
"    def __init__(self):\n"
"        super().__init__('battery_monitor')\n"
"        self.level = 100\n"
"        self.warn_threshold = 30\n"
"        self.error_threshold = 10\n"
"        self.warned = False\n"
"        self.errored = False\n"
"\n"
"        self.get_logger().info(\n"
"            f'Battery monitor started, initial level {self.level}%')\n"
"        self.timer = self.create_timer(0.5, self.timer_callback)\n"
"\n"
"    def timer_callback(self):\n"
"        self.get_logger().debug(f'Battery level: {self.level}%')\n"
"\n"
"        if self.level <= 0:\n"
"            self.get_logger().fatal(\n"
"                'Battery depleted, shutting down battery monitor')\n"
"            raise SystemExit\n"
"\n"
"        if self.level <= self.error_threshold and not self.errored:\n"
"            self.get_logger().error(\n"
"                f'Battery critically low at {self.level}%, stop "
"immediately')\n"
"            self.errored = True\n"
"        elif self.level <= self.warn_threshold and not self.warned:\n"
"            self.get_logger().warning(\n"
"                'Battery low, please return to dock')\n"
"            self.warned = True\n"
"\n"
"        self.level -= 5\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def main(args=None):\n"
"    rclpy.init(args=args)\n"
"    node = BatteryMonitor()\n"
"    try:\n"
"        rclpy.spin(node)\n"
"    except (SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt):\n"
"        pass\n"
"    finally:\n"
"        node.get_logger().info('Battery monitor shutting down')\n"
"        node.destroy_node()\n"
"        if rclpy.ok():\n"
"            rclpy.shutdown()\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"if __name__ == '__main__':\n"
"    main()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:135
msgid "The node does the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:137
msgid "On startup, it logs ``INFO`` with the initial battery level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:138
msgid ""
"Every 0.5 second, it logs ``DEBUG`` with the current reading and drains the "
"battery by 5 %."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:139
msgid "The first time the level reaches 30 % or below, it logs ``WARN``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:140
msgid "The first time the level reaches 10 % or below, it logs ``ERROR``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:141
msgid ""
"When the level reaches 0 %, it logs ``FATAL``, then the node shuts down and "
"logs ``INFO`` on the way out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:143
msgid ""
"``WARN`` and ``ERROR`` are printed only the first time each threshold is "
"crossed, so the terminal stays readable. ``DEBUG`` is printed on every timer "
"callback. Because it is verbose, it is hidden by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:148
msgid "3 Add an entry point"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:150
msgid ""
