#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:199
msgid "5 Run the node with the default log level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:201
msgid ""
"Run the node with no log-level override. That shows which severities appear "
"under the default filter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:204
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:280
msgid "$ ros2 run battery_logging battery_monitor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:208
msgid ""
"The node runs until the battery reaches 0 % and then shuts down. You should "
"see output similar to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:211
msgid ""
"[INFO] [battery_monitor]: Battery monitor started, initial level 100%\n"
"[WARN] [battery_monitor]: Battery low, please return to dock\n"
"[ERROR] [battery_monitor]: Battery critically low at 10%, stop immediately\n"
"[FATAL] [battery_monitor]: Battery depleted, shutting down battery monitor\n"
"[INFO] [battery_monitor]: Battery monitor shutting down"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:219
msgid ""
"Notice that there are no ``DEBUG`` lines for each battery reading. By "
"default, ROS shows ``INFO`` and higher (``WARN``, ``ERROR``, ``FATAL``). "
"``DEBUG`` is below that default, so the per-callback readings stay hidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:224
msgid "6 Reveal DEBUG logs with the CLI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:226
msgid ""
"When you ran the node with no log-level override, it created a ``DEBUG`` "
"message for each battery reading, but the default log level hid those "
"messages. To print them, set the log level to ``debug`` when you start the "
"node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:229
msgid ""
"Run the ``battery_monitor`` with the arguments that allow you to see its "
"``DEBUG`` messages without also printing messages from internal library "
"loggers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:231
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run battery_logging battery_monitor --ros-args --log-level "
"battery_monitor:=debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:235
msgid "Now you should also see a stream of lines such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:237
msgid ""
"[DEBUG] [battery_monitor]: Battery level: 100%\n"
"[DEBUG] [battery_monitor]: Battery level: 95%\n"
"[DEBUG] [battery_monitor]: Battery level: 90%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:243
msgid ""
"The node was already creating those messages. The CLI log level only "
"controls whether they are printed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:246
msgid "Set a global log level to ``debug``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:248
msgid "$ ros2 run battery_logging battery_monitor --ros-args --log-level debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:252
msgid ""
"A global ``debug`` setting applies to every logger in the process, not only "
"``battery_monitor``. Global settings include internal ROS libraries such as "
"``rcl``, so you may see many extra ``DEBUG`` lines that are unrelated to the "
"battery monitor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:255
msgid ""
"If you want global ``DEBUG`` for your own code, set ``rcl`` back to ``info`` "
"to hide the ``rcl`` lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:257
msgid "Other library loggers may still print."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:259
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run battery_logging battery_monitor --ros-args --log-level debug --"
"log-level rcl:=info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:264
msgid "7 Choose an appropriate severity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:266
msgid ""
"The CLI only controls which messages are shown. The severity you pick in "
"code is what operators see by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:269
msgid ""
"In ``battery_monitor.py``, change the low-battery call from ``warning`` to "
"``debug``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:271
msgid ""
"self.get_logger().debug(\n"
"    'Battery low, please return to dock')"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:276
msgid ""
"Return to the root of your workspace, then rebuild the package and source "
"the overlay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:278
msgid "Run the node with no log-level override:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:284
msgid ""
"The battery still crosses 30 %, but the low-battery message no longer "
"appears."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:288
msgid ""
"A real problem logged at ``DEBUG`` stays hidden until someone sets the log "
"level to ``debug``. If you put too many routine messages at ``INFO``, "
"operators may struggle to spot the important ones among them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:291
msgid ""
"In ``battery_monitor.py``, change the call back to ``warning``, then rebuild "
"the package and source the overlay."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:293
msgid "Use this node as a model for when each level fits:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:295
msgid ""
"``DEBUG``: frequent detail that helps while diagnosing a problem, but is too "
"verbose for normal operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:296
msgid ""
"``INFO``: routine lifecycle or status that operators usually want to see."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:297
msgid ""
"``WARN``: something is wrong, but the system can continue if the operator "
"responds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:298
msgid "``ERROR``: a serious fault that needs immediate attention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:299
msgid "``FATAL``: the node cannot continue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:303
msgid ""
"Logging ``FATAL`` does not stop the process by itself. This example raises "
"``SystemExit`` after the fatal message so that the node shuts down cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:307
msgid "8 Inspect the same logs in ``rqt_console``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:309
msgid ""
"Log messages are not limited to the terminal. They are also published on the "
"``/rosout`` topic, so you can view and filter them in a GUI with :doc:`Using "
"rqt_console <../Using-Rqt-Console/Using-Rqt-Console>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:312
msgid "In a new terminal, start ``rqt_console``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:314
msgid "$ ros2 run rqt_console rqt_console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:318
msgid ""
"In another terminal, run the battery monitor with ``--log-level "
"battery_monitor:=debug``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:320
msgid ""
"In ``rqt_console``, exclude ``Debug`` and confirm that the remaining "
"messages match the terminal output from the default log-level run."
msgstr ""

