msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:342
msgid "Why do I not see DEBUG messages when I first run the battery monitor?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:343
msgid ""
"By default, ROS shows log severities of ``INFO`` and above. ``DEBUG`` is "
"below that default, so those messages are generated but not printed. Run the "
"node with ``--ros-args --log-level battery_monitor:=debug`` to show them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:347
msgid "What is the difference between WARN, ERROR, and FATAL?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:348
msgid ""
"``WARN`` means there is a problem the operator can still recover from, such "
"as a low battery. ``ERROR`` means a serious fault that needs immediate "
"action. ``FATAL`` means the node cannot continue. In this tutorial, the node "
"logs ``FATAL`` at 0 % and then shuts itself down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:353
msgid "Does logging FATAL automatically stop my node?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:354
msgid ""
"No. ``FATAL`` is only a severity level for the message. Your code must still "
"stop timers, destroy the node, or shut down ``rclpy`` if the process should "
"exit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:358
msgid "Why do I see many rcl DEBUG lines when I use ``--log-level debug``?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:359
msgid ""
"A global ``debug`` level applies to more loggers than your node alone, "
"including internal ``rcl`` loggers. Narrow the setting with ``--log-level "
"battery_monitor:=debug``, or hide ``rcl`` ``DEBUG`` messages with ``--log-"
"level debug --log-level rcl:=info``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:362
msgid "How do I change the log level when I run a node?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Learning-About-Logging/Learning-About-Logging.rst:363
msgid ""
"Pass ROS arguments after ``--ros-args``. For example: ``ros2 run "
"battery_logging battery_monitor --ros-args --log-level "
"battery_monitor:=debug``."
msgstr ""
